**Given:**

The P alone can complete a work in = 25 days

The Q alone can complete a work in = 50 days

**Formula used:**

Work = Efficiency × Time

**Calculation:**

Let the work completed in 12 days is X percentage.

One day work of P = {1over25}

One day work of Q = {1over50}

One day work of P and Q together = {1over25}+{1over50}={2+1over50}={3over50}

The 12 days of the work = 12times {3over50} = {18over25}

The percentage of work has completed = {18over25}times 100 = 18times 4 = 72\%

**∴ The required result will be 72%.**
